{"id":"319af4f1-2370-4347-afe3-1937752a38f5","expr":"result != null","rationale":"Since the method creates a new Properties object and returns it, result cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.core.io.support.PropertiesLoaderUtils#loadProperties(EncodedResource):Properties","file":"org/springframework/core/io/support/PropertiesLoaderUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T04:54:25.110077699Z"}
{"id":"1cd61b3c-7860-4186-8153-ccfed382b34b","expr":"!result.isEmpty() || result.size() == 0","rationale":"The returned Properties object may be empty or contain entries, so no assumption that it must be non-empty.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.core.io.support.PropertiesLoaderUtils#loadProperties(EncodedResource):Properties","file":"org/springframework/core/io/support/PropertiesLoaderUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T04:54:25.110077699Z"}
{"id":"76805ae6-757a-4a87-9850-af13fc057e2e","expr":"Objects.equals(result.getProperty(\"\"), null) || result.getProperty(\"\") == null","rationale":"It's typical that Properties loaded from a valid resource do not contain empty string keys.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.core.io.support.PropertiesLoaderUtils#loadProperties(EncodedResource):Properties","file":"org/springframework/core/io/support/PropertiesLoaderUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T04:54:25.110077699Z"}
{"id":"f6716a83-6e10-40db-9eda-3893c6ee88fc","expr":"props != null && resource != null && resource.getResource() != null && resource.getEncoding() != null || resource.getEncoding() == null && props.size() >= 0","rationale":"Since fillProperties loads props from resource, if resource and its encoding are not null, props should contain properties.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.core.io.support.PropertiesLoaderUtils#fillProperties(Properties,EncodedResource):void","file":"org/springframework/core/io/support/PropertiesLoaderUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T04:54:25.948393941Z"}
{"id":"04e5058e-f2ea-435b-9730-08c4b140eacb","expr":"props.size() >= 0","rationale":"Properties object size is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.core.io.support.PropertiesLoaderUtils#fillProperties(Properties,EncodedResource):void","file":"org/springframework/core/io/support/PropertiesLoaderUtils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T04:54:25.948393941Z"}
