{"id":"1a2c1d3a-9c05-4393-a3c3-61e501b1170e","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes for bytecode instructions are generally non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.904558048Z"}
{"id":"d8fa9d48-940b-45ac-8826-a3501ca6c620","expr":"operand >= 0","rationale":"Operands for visitIntInsn usually represent constants or offsets which are non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.904558048Z"}
