{"id":"fc99ff73-581a-47fa-9972-9f05fea8cd78","expr":"opcode <= 255","rationale":"Opcode values are defined within a byte range (0 to 255) as per JVM standard.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.904890335Z"}
{"id":"ad90485a-d69d-47ce-a2c7-b9885a21ea1c","expr":"var <= 65535","rationale":"Local variable indices are limited by the JVM's maximum method local variables count, typically up to 65535.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.904890335Z"}
{"id":"c837d61e-bf5e-454d-b58f-fd33bc4cf2d8","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"Variable instructions generally have meaningful opcode values, not nop (0).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.904890335Z"}
{"id":"bde3120b-ae00-49a0-b526-18c9bb2ed71b","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode often represents JVM instruction codes that are non-negative integers.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.913631937Z"}
{"id":"db41da34-4131-4310-a776-0263184248cd","expr":"desc != null","rationale":"The descriptor string passed to visitTypeInsn cannot be null as it is used in method calls.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.913631937Z"}
{"id":"a0865ac0-1b37-4c4d-bdc7-fa12ba5517ee","expr":"!desc.isEmpty()","rationale":"Typically, type descriptors must be non-empty strings indicating JVM types.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.913631937Z"}
{"id":"98302229-849a-4de5-abcd-045d48f7bc76","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"The opcode parameter should be a valid JVM opcode which are typically non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.914331416Z"}
{"id":"3941a9c7-5899-4804-a200-13ef01cf2177","expr":"var >= 0","rationale":"The var parameter represents a local variable index which must be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.914331416Z"}
{"id":"e45f46e7-394f-41d0-9753-d4289e0f65b8","expr":"(opcode != 169) || var >= 0","rationale":"For the RET opcode (169), the var must be a valid non-negative local variable index.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.914331416Z"}
{"id":"a06b1352-07a8-44e0-ab37-4e0e2ecb97fc","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"visitVarInsn should only be called with opcodes corresponding to variable instructions, which are not zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.914331416Z"}
{"id":"bf712f97-bef7-453d-bbc6-9453202c3e6b","expr":"var < 65536","rationale":"The var index is limited by JVM to a maximum of 65535 as these are usually represented with unsigned short.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.914331416Z"}
{"id":"3f6f89f2-bc02-44de-83ce-e6df25237288","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"opcode should represent a valid bytecode instruction value.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.cglib.transform.MethodVisitorTee#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/cglib/transform/MethodVisitorTee.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:05:06.922780487Z"}
