{"id":"0c389a0e-30a2-47d1-a4a2-86b15a364f00","expr":"type == 0 || type == 1 || type == 2 || type == 3 || type == 4 || type == 5","rationale":"The frame type must be one of the predefined constants (e.g., Opcodes.F_NEW, F_FULL, etc.).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFrame(int,int,Object[],int,Object[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.090679123Z"}
{"id":"cf291624-e78c-4687-ac0d-390ec2cb762f","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes in ASM are typically non-negative integers corresponding to opcode values.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.173917476Z"}
{"id":"019df55f-8274-4cb1-9458-613fba276b9b","expr":"opcode < 256","rationale":"ASM opcodes fit within a byte, so they must be less than 256.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.173917476Z"}
{"id":"53f8c2aa-aae5-4026-b7a4-b053582b1887","expr":"operand >= -32768 && operand <= 65535","rationale":"Operand is likely constrained to fit in 16-bit range for these instructions.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIntInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.198645873Z"}
{"id":"5960e588-d86d-4bec-9256-505e91b3a2f7","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"Opcode values are expected within the unsigned byte range, consistent with standard JVM opcode ranges.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInsn(int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.205999806Z"}
{"id":"2c05fea1-686f-436e-bd96-29b27a0034a4","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indices are non-negative indices.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.300893706Z"}
{"id":"eb9a1b25-372d-44ef-b057-9776c1335e3e","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode should be non-negative as valid instruction codes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.300893706Z"}
{"id":"f67f0a75-7139-4763-b3af-72d99b79bc57","expr":"varIndex < 256 || varIndex >= 256","rationale":"Either varIndex is below 256 or at least 256 to choose encoding path.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.300893706Z"}
{"id":"7f3c106a-d34c-47f4-81b6-d7ac21a3cbdb","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode values represent instruction codes, typically non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.332454195Z"}
{"id":"dd9a32a3-0db9-4e46-bb3e-985575e0d350","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Variable indexes in bytecode are always zero or positive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitVarInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.332454195Z"}
{"id":"4a4ef627-20ec-4bfc-bce7-9680fc6ea05b","expr":"type != null","rationale":"The type parameter is used by symbolTable.addConstantClass(type), which requires type to be non-null","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.375376804Z"}
{"id":"0f866d32-558d-47bc-9bd3-de80193c305f","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcodes represent instruction codes and are usually non-negative integers","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.375376804Z"}
{"id":"ae167f20-c93f-431c-96c1-fc0eb27548db","expr":"opcode <= 255","rationale":"Java bytecodes opcodes are defined as 1-byte unsigned values, so their values are between 0 and 255 inclusive","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.375376804Z"}
{"id":"9a19a59d-ee75-441d-a9bb-181db7084510","expr":"!type.isEmpty()","rationale":"The type string represents a class name and should not be empty","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.375376804Z"}
{"id":"e7f6377a-7557-4084-a1df-ca0897f7d5a7","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"The opcode parameter corresponds to JVM opcode values which are typically in the range 0 to 255.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.396740407Z"}
{"id":"07188e0a-667c-4fb3-bf72-b912f2ba077e","expr":"type != null && !type.isEmpty()","rationale":"The type argument, representing a class/type descriptor, should be a valid non-null non-empty string.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.396740407Z"}
{"id":"0ea8d333-3e9c-4ae8-9de4-9f0b58e0f021","expr":"!type.contains(\" \")","rationale":"The internal name provided by 'type' is expected to be a valid descriptor without spaces.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTypeInsn(int,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.396740407Z"}
{"id":"19ecb015-dc6b-4ed9-b51b-d65ac0858603","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The internal name of the class owning the field should be a valid (non-null) string.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.440159038Z"}
{"id":"5e164c87-4013-4379-8f92-6d5bc63b2e4c","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The name of the field should be non-null as a valid identifier.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.440159038Z"}
{"id":"02f958cc-1d0a-47c4-96c2-9526d4d8db3b","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The field descriptor is mandatory and must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.440159038Z"}
{"id":"e0a7ecab-3e65-4ebb-938e-7ade2327f910","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"Opcodes in the JVM bytecode are in the range 0 to 255 (byte values).","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.440159038Z"}
{"id":"5a8b6c3e-81dd-448f-b618-4ffe2f1488d1","expr":"(opcode == 178 || opcode == 179 || opcode == 180 || opcode == 181)","rationale":"The method deals with field instructions, so opcode must be one of the four related opcodes.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.440159038Z"}
{"id":"4cbc8f33-e76c-4ccc-901c-1f47d439e06e","expr":"opcode == 178 || opcode == 179 || opcode == 180 || opcode == 181","rationale":"The opcode corresponds to one of the GETSTATIC, PUTSTATIC, GETFIELD, or PUTFIELD instructions.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.484099550Z"}
{"id":"abd8598e-b6f0-4fa3-83bf-8f567e92de0d","expr":"owner != null && name != null && descriptor != null","rationale":"The method requires non-null owner, name, and descriptor strings to add fieldref symbol.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.484099550Z"}
{"id":"c343104e-6381-42fd-bc05-8aebeb081539","expr":"(opcode == 178 || opcode == 179) || (opcode == 180 || opcode == 181)","rationale":"The opcode partitions into static (GETSTATIC, PUTSTATIC) and instance (GETFIELD, PUTFIELD) field instructions.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitFieldInsn(int,String,String,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.484099550Z"}
{"id":"e7df44b0-ea4b-40f0-acb3-00bd397c6bf9","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The owner parameter is the internal name of the method's owner class and must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.506991508Z"}
{"id":"7ea2c4e5-10e1-4ee3-b115-97e9a068f010","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The method name identifies the method and should always be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.506991508Z"}
{"id":"c617cdf2-e196-4368-86d4-7d89f999692d","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The method descriptor describes the types of arguments and return value and hence must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.506991508Z"}
{"id":"b103a9d1-c173-4428-92e4-b64b8fa3ea3d","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"The opcode parameter represents a JVM bytecode instruction and is expected to be non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.506991508Z"}
{"id":"f1f6f7bd-ac11-42ec-af43-34670f0e4302","expr":"(opcode == 185) == isInterface","rationale":"If the opcode indicates an interface method invocation, the isInterface boolean should be true, otherwise false.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.562343253Z"}
{"id":"350a62fd-0985-4262-9bef-a72cfea2745b","expr":"owner != null","rationale":"The owner of the method invoked should be a valid class name string and should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.562343253Z"}
{"id":"d60d9db3-45f0-4df2-b736-1a596304c921","expr":"name != null && name.length() > 0","rationale":"The method name must be a valid non-empty string to represent the invoked method.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.562343253Z"}
{"id":"6529f572-31d6-43b3-9394-66b608b9c4b8","expr":"descriptor != null && descriptor.length() > 0","rationale":"Method descriptor is expected to be valid non-empty string describing the method signature.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.562343253Z"}
{"id":"6841a2f5-6a9b-475e-8237-69f26a0b8e79","expr":"opcode != 0","rationale":"Opcode should be a valid JVM instruction opcode and is unlikely to be zero at this point in the code.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMethodInsn(int,String,String,String,boolean):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.562343253Z"}
{"id":"899ea2e6-639a-4259-a307-bb39937ea0c7","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The name parameter should represent a method or field name and thus must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.607729272Z"}
{"id":"b3ba0d6e-4e1f-49ca-b89a-839c69cf0f56","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor defines the method type descriptor and must always be present.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.607729272Z"}
{"id":"8d98850a-249d-4389-8447-b382df172423","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"The bootstrap method handle is essential for resolving the invoke dynamic call site.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.607729272Z"}
{"id":"bea0aceb-1747-4562-bb63-13abab3bae6e","expr":"bootstrapMethodArguments == null || bootstrapMethodArguments.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"Bootstrap method arguments represent varargs and are modeled as Object, so they must be an array type or null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.607729272Z"}
{"id":"15570cd4-cbc3-4a76-836b-79afd963c017","expr":"name != null","rationale":"The name of the method or dynamic call must be non-null for the invoke dynamic instruction to be valid.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.622332059Z"}
{"id":"504f6dd6-a349-43eb-998e-f5d2208fc8b0","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"Because the method descriptor is fundamental to the bytecode instruction, it should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.622332059Z"}
{"id":"11566401-ee1a-4ed1-b200-53a4d25908f6","expr":"bootstrapMethodHandle != null","rationale":"This handle is necessary to create the constant invoke dynamic symbol.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.622332059Z"}
{"id":"17e82d03-e7c1-428d-9bec-8f2c7acb12e4","expr":"bootstrapMethodArguments == null || bootstrapMethodArguments.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length properties are always non-negative but this confirms non-null or empty args are possible.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitInvokeDynamicInsn(String,String,Handle,Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.622332059Z"}
{"id":"28d96a61-6236-48c1-95bf-81d6ccecfd1b","expr":"opcode >= 0","rationale":"Opcode values are generally non-negative integers representing bytecode instructions","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.686948408Z"}
{"id":"356929ae-98db-43be-8ec5-bb548c00dd6c","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label parameter must be non-null because label.flags and label.put are accessed without null checks.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.723166928Z"}
{"id":"4add5d9b-a8d8-46f9-a863-1d69c29f0511","expr":"label.flags >= 0","rationale":"Label flags are used in bitwise operations which are typically non-negative flags.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.723166928Z"}
{"id":"641a5979-3af5-464c-9135-34e0c4437e55","expr":"opcode >= 0 && opcode <= 255","rationale":"In JVM bytecode, opcodes are between 0 and 255 inclusive.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitJumpInsn(int,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.723166928Z"}
{"id":"0205d4f7-25df-4916-9575-36dfda3aa34a","expr":"label != null","rationale":"The label parameter should never be null as it represents the label to be visited.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.739660477Z"}
{"id":"308a01c6-c063-497c-8eb7-22608156d57c","expr":"label.flags >= 0","rationale":"Flags usually represent bit flags, so negative values don't make sense.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.739660477Z"}
{"id":"df4b8aa7-7fa8-41ee-8123-61e512594d2e","expr":"label.bytecodeOffset >= 0","rationale":"Labels represent a position in bytecode, which is never negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.739660477Z"}
{"id":"32bb328e-9782-467c-9889-111ddb9cffd0","expr":"label.frame == null || label.frame.owner == label","rationale":"From the context, label.frame is either null or has owner field pointing to label; this maintains frame ownership consistency.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.739660477Z"}
{"id":"b7fddbc1-b9be-43bc-a8e6-681ac96467c9","expr":"label != null","rationale":"Label must be non-null at method exit.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.810901925Z"}
{"id":"1a84cacd-7f34-4647-bafe-6bcbb65620ef","expr":"label.frame == null || label.frame.owner == label","rationale":"The frame owner is updated to label or label.frame can be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.810901925Z"}
{"id":"07824372-dec8-4982-98ea-b881d9308cb7","expr":"label.bytecodeOffset >= 0","rationale":"Basic blocks and labels alignment imply non-negative bytecode offset.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLabel(Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.810901925Z"}
{"id":"745ea283-b9b0-46a3-a363-dd7d0b01b32b","expr":"value != null","rationale":"The value passed to visitLdcInsn is typically a constant to be added; expecting non-null is common though null may be allowed.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.838629350Z"}
{"id":"c5f172ab-048d-4d97-82db-370359c78cde","expr":"value != null || value == null","rationale":"value parameter may be null or non-null based on user input or caller context.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.856789086Z"}
{"id":"1efdf405-11d7-496a-933a-8d2c5b97d6c5","expr":"value == null || value.getClass() != null","rationale":"If value is non-null, calling getClass() is safe and returns non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.856789086Z"}
{"id":"b364db41-5df0-4e27-9b1d-3d212d275740","expr":"value == null || value.toString().length() >= 0","rationale":"Ensures that for non-null value, calling toString and length is safe and well-defined.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLdcInsn(Object):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.856789086Z"}
{"id":"14fd294c-d6b2-4d37-9ff9-9d8cd4609892","expr":"varIndex >= 0","rationale":"Local variable indexes in bytecode are non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.922439139Z"}
{"id":"bad10ed2-d043-492f-a5b0-bdc05f0da3dd","expr":"increment <= 127","rationale":"Increment values fit in a signed byte range for the non-wide case.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.922439139Z"}
{"id":"7e81406b-6326-4d3a-bcb2-e22d0bf0d60b","expr":"increment >= -128","rationale":"Increment values fit in a signed byte range for the non-wide case.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.922439139Z"}
{"id":"b66492d9-9a78-4d4c-ad06-2c0402d5367e","expr":"(varIndex > 255) || (increment > 127) || (increment < -128)","rationale":"The method uses the WIDE instruction if any of these conditions is true.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.922439139Z"}
{"id":"93d7c25f-dc63-494b-87d9-86ddc615675a","expr":"varIndex <= 65535","rationale":"VarIndex when wide encoded must fit in a short according to standard JVM constraints.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.922439139Z"}
{"id":"d9806c60-c772-4195-b673-0a37e9048aec","expr":"(varIndex >= 0)","rationale":"Local variable index should be non-negative as it refers to a variable slot in the frame.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.955395811Z"}
{"id":"3abdbe49-39b2-4812-a7e1-163b879b2f09","expr":"(increment >= -128 && increment <= 127) || (varIndex > 255)","rationale":"If varIndex > 255 or increment is out of the range [-128, 127], the WIDE instruction is used.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.955395811Z"}
{"id":"fa3b75f6-4c01-41df-b077-020f5d7f98f5","expr":"varIndex < 256 || increment < -128 || increment > 127","rationale":"If varIndex is below or equal 255 and increment fits in signed byte, WIDE not used.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.955395811Z"}
{"id":"2de76469-fd97-4f74-883e-e9874a2e3c2c","expr":"increment >= -128 && increment <= 127","rationale":"Increment value for IINC must fit in signed byte if WIDE prefix is not used.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.955395811Z"}
{"id":"2e73193b-ff05-415d-9fd8-8c7dea595825","expr":"varIndex + 1 >= 1","rationale":"maxLocals is updated if current varIndex + 1 is greater than existing maxLocals, thus varIndex + 1 >= 1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitIincInsn(int,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.955395811Z"}
{"id":"835a3e28-3cdc-4ae4-92cf-11b791271783","expr":"min <= max","rationale":"In a tableswitch instruction, the min bytecode value is always less than or equal to max to define a valid switch case range.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.968466176Z"}
{"id":"1fc5295d-fe0f-496b-a6e1-c60558e8a783","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels parameter cannot be null because the method iterates over labels to put them to the code.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.968466176Z"}
{"id":"41809cdd-0d53-4fa2-8175-8439650b5776","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"The label array should contain exactly one Label entry per possible switch value between min and max.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.968466176Z"}
{"id":"9e24dadd-b763-45bd-ab76-7ee5cce5163f","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is used for all keys not covered by the range and labels, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:05.968466176Z"}
{"id":"08fd464d-7c3a-4d0d-8c98-d8987fd21ac2","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array is documented as a varargs parameter and used in a loop and method calls, so it cannot be null here.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.031012813Z"}
{"id":"0b3b7588-e03b-442e-8f48-7aaed978b31e","expr":"labels.length == max - min + 1","rationale":"A table switch requires a label for each value from min to max inclusive, so labels length equals max-min+1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.031012813Z"}
{"id":"508de2fd-e5ba-409d-82d0-ac2875879510","expr":"min <= max","rationale":"A table switch instruction requires a valid range with min <= max to be meaningful.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.031012813Z"}
{"id":"7f110524-56e9-4070-bbc7-6639fee26760","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"Since dflt.put() is called, dflt cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.031012813Z"}
{"id":"3204644e-d99c-4f05-a7b7-8aa77e3b70bf","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Though trivial, this asserts labels array length is not negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTableSwitchInsn(int,int,Label,Label):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.031012813Z"}
{"id":"9adccb2d-e6ac-4b58-b149-fc33a1f94319","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"A lookup switch instruction must have a valid default label.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.066460878Z"}
{"id":"2cf3b1a3-0a39-4075-9ddb-2de6a337d51a","expr":"keys != null && labels != null","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays are essential for the lookup switch and cannot be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.066460878Z"}
{"id":"8c137092-5ff7-44cc-9a68-622d77d35f9d","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"Each key has a corresponding label, so the lengths must match.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.066460878Z"}
{"id":"3eae227a-476c-494c-91ba-0c70ed75c31f","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Array length can't be negative; labels.length must be >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.066460878Z"}
{"id":"b983cb4f-a6b0-47f3-965b-ad6de71b49fd","expr":"keys != null && labels != null","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays are required and assumed non-null to support iteration and processing.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.078821856Z"}
{"id":"d2829fc7-1504-4224-aaf6-88daf23f6050","expr":"keys.length == labels.length","rationale":"The keys and labels arrays represent a mapping from keys to labels; they must be of equal length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.078821856Z"}
{"id":"ef31f9bc-a978-4ccd-b624-637165ebb8b7","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is needed for the switch instruction and should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.078821856Z"}
{"id":"ded1609e-1ac8-4b40-97bc-3e764744655d","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Array lengths are non-negative by definition.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.078821856Z"}
{"id":"97fd78b6-00fc-40d3-862d-34debabf7751","expr":"keys.length >= 0","rationale":"Array lengths are non-negative by definition.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitLookupSwitchInsn(Label,int[],Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.078821856Z"}
{"id":"bd53795a-72ae-49f9-b20b-34238354fdfc","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label must be provided and is used immediately.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.141022064Z"}
{"id":"5997b7e5-7953-407e-b8a8-b637ce35a77c","expr":"labels != null","rationale":"The labels array must be provided to add successors.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.141022064Z"}
{"id":"031a1764-79d3-4f1e-8e41-b91e38b61f26","expr":"labels.length >= 0","rationale":"Labels is an array, so length is non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.141022064Z"}
{"id":"89f5af35-66a3-449f-ba58-0d41509b77fe","expr":"dflt.getCanonicalInstance() != null","rationale":"The method calls getCanonicalInstance on dflt and expects it non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.141022064Z"}
{"id":"6df3e8ea-4c90-4dbc-a1b9-dd9df256f4e5","expr":"dflt != null","rationale":"The default label is always used as a successor and its flag is set, so it must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.172737136Z"}
{"id":"659854ca-9699-4fe9-b1e5-22981376f845","expr":"labels != null && labels.length > 0","rationale":"Labels array is iterated over to add successors and set flags, so it must be non-null with at least one element.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.172737136Z"}
{"id":"ebbadabf-39f7-4ca4-aa51-9eb0d1a1083a","expr":"dflt.getCanonicalInstance() != null","rationale":"A canonical instance is accessed and flags updated, so must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitSwitchInsn(Label,Label[]):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.172737136Z"}
{"id":"a2241be4-9426-4d95-940e-830edd84daca","expr":"descriptor != null","rationale":"The descriptor string must be non-null as it is used to add a constant class.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.190598555Z"}
{"id":"e30fe0a8-51ef-46dc-b807-3db763d89c90","expr":"numDimensions >= 1","rationale":"The number of dimensions for a new multi-array must be at least one.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitMultiANewArrayInsn(String,int):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.190598555Z"}
