{"id":"a89c71f5-93a6-4769-bd5f-0c324d289a39","expr":"handler != null","rationale":"The handler Label is used directly in the Handler constructor and thus must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.386957131Z"}
{"id":"1497b542-ed7f-4355-b4f3-525deee5bf37","expr":"(start.position < end.position)","rationale":"In a try-catch block, the start label must precede the end label, so start.position < end.position should hold.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.springframework.asm.MethodWriter#visitTryCatchBlock(Label,Label,Label,String):void","file":"org/springframework/asm/MethodWriter.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T05:06:06.386957131Z"}
